<FPReturnValueCtrl>
<DisplayFormat>kfpHex</DisplayFormat>
</FPReturnValueCtrl>
</FPCtrl>
</FPPanel>
</FPNodeTypeWindow>
<FPNodeTypeWindow name="Configure Reflection Measurement Amplitude">
<DOSHelpText/>
<FPPanel functionName="ConfigureReflectionMeasurementAmplitude">
<FnPos>0</FnPos>
<XPos>1</XPos>
<YPos>17</YPos>
<Height>331</Height>
<Width>558</Width>
<PanelDisabledByDefault>kfpFalse</PanelDisabledByDefault>
<UseScrollBars>kfpFalse</UseScrollBars>
<FunctionQualifier>
</FunctionQualifier>
<HelpText>Configures the Auto Scale State, Amplitude Scale Reference Level, Amplitude Scale Per Division for reflection measurement.

Note:
This function is applicable for N9321C, N9322C, N9323C and N9324C models.</HelpText>
<FPCtrl label="Instrument Handle">
<XPos>25</XPos>
<YPos>301</YPos>
<CtrlWidth>145</CtrlWidth>
<ParamPosition>1</ParamPosition>
<CtrlDataTypeIfBuiltIn/>
<CtrlDataTypeIfUserDefined>ViSession</CtrlDataTypeIfUserDefined>
<HelpText>The ViSession handle that you obtain from the agn934xni_init or agn934xni_InitWithOptions function.  The handle identifies a particular instrument session.

Default Value: None</HelpText>
<FPInputCtrl>
<DefaultValue>
</DefaultValue>
</FPInputCtrl>
</FPCtrl>
<FPCtrl label="Auto Scale">
<XPos>80</XPos>
<YPos>45</YPos>
<CtrlWidth>145</CtrlWidth>
<ParamPosition>2</ParamPosition>
<CtrlDataTypeIfBuiltIn/>
<CtrlDataTypeIfUserDefined>ViBoolean</CtrlDataTypeIfUserDefined>
<HelpText>Enables or disables amplitude auto scale once if it is set to VI_TURE.

Valid Values:
VI_TRUE: Enable
VI_FALSE: Disable

Default Value: VI_FALSE

Command:
CAT:SCALe:AUTO</HelpText>
<FPBinaryCtrl>
<DefaultValue>kfpOff</DefaultValue>
<OffValue label="False">VI_FALSE</OffValue>
<OnValue label="True">VI_TRUE</OnValue>
</FPBinaryCtrl>
</FPCtrl>
<FPCtrl label="Reference Level">
<XPos>206</XPos>
<YPos>45</YPos>
<CtrlWidth>145</CtrlWidth>
<ParamPosition>3</ParamPosition>
<CtrlDataTypeIfBuiltIn/>
<CtrlDataTypeIfUserDefined>ViReal64</CtrlDataTypeIfUserDefined>
<HelpText>Sets the amplitude scale reference level.

The driver uses this value to set the AGN934XNI_ATTR_REFLECTION_MEASUREMENT_AMPLITUDE_SCALE_REFERENCE_LEVEL attribute.

Valid Range:
Min: 1 dB
Max: 60 dB

Default Value: 1.05 dB

Note:
Valid only when Auto Scale is VI_FALSE.

Command:
[:SENSe]:CAT:SCALe:REFerence &lt;value&gt;</HelpText>
<FPInputCtrl>
<DefaultValue>1.05</DefaultValue>
</FPInputCtrl>
</FPCtrl>
<FPCtrl label="Scale Per Division">
<XPos>387</XPos>
<YPos>45</YPos>
<CtrlWidth>145</CtrlWidth>
<ParamPosition>4</ParamPosition>
<CtrlDataTypeIfBuiltIn/>
<CtrlDataTypeIfUserDefined>ViReal64</CtrlDataTypeIfUserDefined>
<HelpText>Sets the amplitude display scale per division.

The driver uses this value to set the AGN934XNI_ATTR_REFLECTION_MEASUREMENT_AMPLITUDE_SCALE_PER_DIVISION attribute.

Valid Range:
Min: 0.1 dB
Max: 10 dB

Default Value: 0.1 dB

Note:
Valid only when Auto Scale is VI_FALSE.

Command:
[:SENSe]:CAT:SCALe:DIV &lt;value&gt;</HelpText>
<FPInputCtrl>
<DefaultValue>0.1</DefaultValue>
</FPInputCtrl>
</FPCtrl>
<FPCtrl label="Status">
<XPos>387</XPos>
<YPos>291</YPos>
<CtrlWidth>150</CtrlWidth>
<ParamPosition/>
<CtrlDataTypeIfBuiltIn/>
<CtrlDataTypeIfUserDefined>ViStatus</CtrlDataTypeIfUserDefined>
