<FPNodeTypeWindow name="Configure Marker Type">
<DOSHelpText/>
<FPPanel functionName="ConfigureMarkerType">
<FnPos>0</FnPos>
<XPos>1</XPos>
<YPos>17</YPos>
<Height>331</Height>
<Width>558</Width>
<PanelDisabledByDefault>kfpFalse</PanelDisabledByDefault>
<UseScrollBars>kfpFalse</UseScrollBars>
<FunctionQualifier>
</FunctionQualifier>
<HelpText>This function selects the type of markers that you want to activate.

Notes:
The user must call agn934xc_SetActiveMarker function ahead to specify the active marker before calling this function.</HelpText>
<FPCtrl label="Instrument Handle">
<XPos>25</XPos>
<YPos>301</YPos>
<CtrlWidth>145</CtrlWidth>
<ParamPosition>1</ParamPosition>
<CtrlDataTypeIfBuiltIn/>
<CtrlDataTypeIfUserDefined>ViSession</CtrlDataTypeIfUserDefined>
<HelpText>The ViSession handle that you obtain from the agn934xni_init or agn934xni_InitWithOptions function.  The handle identifies a particular instrument session.

Default Value: None</HelpText>
<FPInputCtrl>
<DefaultValue>
</DefaultValue>
</FPInputCtrl>
</FPCtrl>
<FPCtrl label="Marker Type">
<XPos>25</XPos>
<YPos>45</YPos>
<CtrlWidth>145</CtrlWidth>
<ParamPosition>2</ParamPosition>
<CtrlDataTypeIfBuiltIn/>
<CtrlDataTypeIfUserDefined>ViInt32</CtrlDataTypeIfUserDefined>
<HelpText>Selects the type of markers that you want to activate. 
The driver uses this value to set the AGN934XNI_ATTR_MARKER_TYPE attribute.

Valid Values:
AGN934XNI_VAL_MARKER_TYPE_NORMAL: Normal
AGN934XNI_VAL_MARKER_TYPE_DELTA: Delta
AGN934XNI_VAL_MARKER_TYPE_OFF: Off

Default Value: AGN934XNI_VAL_MARKER_TYPE_OFF</HelpText>
<FPRingCtrl>
<DefaultIndex>2</DefaultIndex>
<LabelValue label="Normal">AGN934XNI_VAL_MARKER_TYPE_NORMAL</LabelValue>
<LabelValue label="Delta">AGN934XNI_VAL_MARKER_TYPE_DELTA</LabelValue>
<LabelValue label="Off">AGN934XNI_VAL_MARKER_TYPE_OFF</LabelValue>
</FPRingCtrl>
</FPCtrl>
<FPCtrl label="Marker Function">
<XPos>387</XPos>
<YPos>45</YPos>
<CtrlWidth>145</CtrlWidth>
<ParamPosition>3</ParamPosition>
<CtrlDataTypeIfBuiltIn/>
<CtrlDataTypeIfUserDefined>ViInt32</CtrlDataTypeIfUserDefined>
<HelpText>selects the marker function for the designated marker.
The driver uses this value to set the AGN934XNI_ATTR_MARKER_FUNCTION attribute.

Valid Values:
AGN934XNI_VAL_MARKER_FUNCTION_FCOUNT: Frequency Counter
AGN934XNI_VAL_MARKER_FUNCTION_NOISE: Noise
AGN934XNI_VAL_MARKER_FUNCTION_OFF: Normal

Default Value: AGN934XNI_VAL_MARKER_FUNCTION_OFF</HelpText>
<FPRingCtrl>
<DefaultIndex>2</DefaultIndex>
<LabelValue label="Frequency Counter">AGN934XNI_VAL_MARKER_FUNCTION_FCOUNT</LabelValue>
<LabelValue label="Noise">AGN934XNI_VAL_MARKER_FUNCTION_NOISE</LabelValue>
<LabelValue label="Normal">AGN934XNI_VAL_MARKER_FUNCTION_OFF</LabelValue>
</FPRingCtrl>
</FPCtrl>
