<FPCtrl label="Video Trigger Level">
<XPos>25</XPos>
<YPos>45</YPos>
<CtrlWidth>145</CtrlWidth>
<ParamPosition>2</ParamPosition>
<CtrlDataTypeIfBuiltIn/>
<CtrlDataTypeIfUserDefined>ViReal64</CtrlDataTypeIfUserDefined>
<HelpText>Specifies the level that the video signal shall reach to trigger the acquisition.
The driver uses this value to set the AGN934XNI_ATTR_VIDEO_TRIGGER_LEVEL attribute.

Valid Range: 10 display divisions below reference level to reference level


Default Value: 0</HelpText>
<FPInputCtrl>
<DefaultValue>0</DefaultValue>
</FPInputCtrl>
</FPCtrl>
